"Erewash Borough Council","xy":[-1.30626,52.99627]},"147202":{"h":10,"osm":"way/77122531","kind":"pavilion","council":"Erewash Borough Council","xy":[-1.3066,52.99601]},"147203":{"h":6.5,"base":5,"osm":"way/922758116","kind":"bridge","sum":"Derbyshire Extension Branch is a bridge.","sumSrc":{"title":"OpenStreetMap","kind":"Written from the map's data"},"council":"Broxtowe Borough Council","xy":[-1.29735,52.98981]},"147204":{"h":6.5,"base":5,"osm":"way/16926838","kind":"bridge","qid":"Q4889617","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Bennerley%20Viaduct%20Ilkeston.jpg","article":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bennerley_Viaduct","cat":"Bennerley Viaduct","sum":"Bennerley Viaduct is a former railway bridge, now a foot and cycle bridge, between Ilkeston, Derbyshire, and Awsworth, Nottinghamshire, in central England. It was completed in 1877 and carried the Great Northern Railway's Derbyshire Extension over the River Erewash, which forms the county boundary, and its wide, flat valley. The engineer was Samuel Abbott, who worked under Richard Johnson, the GNR's chief engineer.","sumSrc":{"title":"Bennerley Viaduct","kind":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bennerley_Viaduct"},"council":"Broxtowe Borough Council","xy":[-1.29734,52.9898]},"147205":{"h":5.5,"base":4,"osm":"way/584872269","kind":"bridge","listEntry":1140437,"listUrl":"https://historicengland.org.uk/listing/the-list/list-entry/1140437","qid":"Q4889617","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Bennerley%20Viaduct%20Ilkeston.jpg","article":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bennerley_Viaduct","cat":"Bennerley Viaduct","stories":[{"layer":"bennerley","text":"E. P. Davis built the Bennerley furnaces, near Ilkeston, in about 1870; by 1880 they belonged to the Awsworth Coal and Iron Company, which was putting up a new furnace.[^grace] A branch of the viaduct's railway served the works. They made their last pig iron in March 1931, and in 1934 Thos. W. Ward of Sheffield bought the three furnaces to take them down.[^grace] The pin is approximate.","source":{"title":"Bennerley Viaduct","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bennerley_Viaduct","kind":"Wikipedia"},"cites":{"grace":{"title":"Bennerley Ironworks (Grace's Guide)","url":"https://gracesguide.co.uk/Bennerley_Ironworks","kind":"gracesguide.co.uk","read":"2026-11-16"}},"when":"c. 1870","whenSrc":{"title":"Bennerley Ironworks (Grace's Guide)","url":"https://gracesguide.co.uk/Bennerley_Ironworks","kind":"gracesguide.co.uk","read":"2026-11-16"},"nm":"Bennerley Ironworks"},{"layer":"bennerley","text":"In 1876–77 a viaduct was built here of wrought iron, light enough for ground undermined by coal workings. It closed in 1968 but was too costly to take down, and in 2022 it reopened to walkers and cyclists. The only other viaduct like it is Meldon Viaduct in Devon.","source":{"title":"Bennerley Viaduct","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bennerley_Viaduct","kind":"Wikipedia"},"when":"1877","whenSrc":{"title":"Bennerley Viaduct","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bennerley_Viaduct","kind":"Wikipedia"},"nm":"Bennerley Viaduct"}],"sum":"Bennerley Viaduct is a former railway bridge, now a foot and cycle bridge, between Ilkeston, Derbyshire, and Awsworth, Nottinghamshire, in central England. It was completed in 1877 and carried the Great Northern Railway's Derbyshire Extension over the River Erewash, which forms the county boundary, and its wide, flat valley. The engineer was Samuel Abbott, who worked under Richard Johnson, the GNR's chief engineer.","sumSrc":{"title":"Bennerley Viaduct","kind":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bennerley_Viaduct"},"council":"Broxtowe Borough Council","xy":[-1.29747,52.98976]},"147206":{"h":6.5,"base":5,"osm":"way/365921840","kind":"bridge","council":"Erewash Borough Council","xy":[-1.30021,52.98979]},"147207":{"h":10,"osm":"way/37746752","kind":"pub","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Bridge_Inn%2C_Cotmanhay_-_30_M